WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.254
Open T1 Arc and you can check
your latest glucose reading,

00:00:04.405 --> 00:00:05.624
see which way it's moving,

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.655
and how recently it was updated.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.541
Then you can look at what
else has been happening.

00:00:12.982 --> 00:00:15.675
How you slept, your workouts,
your heart rate.

00:00:16.117 --> 00:00:18.125
Information from your connected apps,

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.656
available here alongside your glucose.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.499
You can also ask Tarv1s about that data,

00:00:24.545 --> 00:00:25.776
in your own words.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.190
Say you want to check
how yesterday went.

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:32.454
You could start with a simple question:

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:34.973
What was my average glucose yesterday?

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.260
Here, the average was six
point six millimoles per litre.

00:00:42.771 --> 00:00:44.733
You can open the readings
behind the answer

00:00:44.791 --> 00:00:46.033
and check what it used.

00:00:46.474 --> 00:00:49.853
It helps explain your records,
not recommend treatment.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.738
To look more closely, open the timeline.

00:00:57.179 --> 00:01:00.871
You can see glucose alongside
meals, insulin and activity,

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.124
and follow what happened
through the day.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.977
And you can keep adding
to that record as you go.

00:01:09.419 --> 00:01:11.566
Search for a food, choose your portion,

00:01:11.648 --> 00:01:14.573
and check the nutritional
details before you save.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.527
T1 Arc is open source.

00:01:22.736 --> 00:01:24.814
Your health history is stored
on your phone.

00:01:25.058 --> 00:01:26.869
We don’t collect your health data.
